      "score": 98,
      "comments": 39,
      "author": "refp",
      "published": "2026-07-25T11:33:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "The POSIX shell colon built-in is a no-op command returning exit status 0 without spawning external subprocesses.",
        "Pair the colon with parameter expansions like ': ${VAR:=default}' to safely set variable defaults without executing the result.",
        "Use the colon for lightweight infinite loops ('while :; do'), script placeholders, and fast file truncation (': > file')."
      ]
